    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly present 3B Durham Road, an impressive four-bedroom house offering approximately 177 sq. m. of exceptionally bright and spacious accommodation over three floors, superbly positioned just moments from Sandymount Village and the Strand. Built in 2012, the property has been thoughtfully designed to maximise natural light, space and energy efficiency with a B energy rating, creating a stylish and comfortable modern home in one of Dublin 4's most desirable neighbourhoods.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor is centred around a superb open-plan living, dining and kitchen space, providing a wonderful setting for both everyday family life and entertaining. A dual aspect allows an abundance of natural light and provide excellent connectivity to the outdoor areas. The contemporary kitchen with an island is fitted with an extensive range of quality Neff and Electrolux appliances, complemented by a separate utility room. The spacious entrance hallway includes a guest WC.\r\n\r\nThe first floor comprises three well-proportioned bedrooms, including one with an en-suite, together with a spacious family bathroom.\r\n\r\nOccupying the entire top floor, the principal bedroom suite is a particular highlight, offering excellent proportions, privacy, a substantial walk-in wardrobe and its own en-suite bathroom. This dedicated upper level gives the house a sense of space and flexibility rarely found in more traditional homes in the area.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property enjoys a private, low-maintenance rear garden with a useful storage room, while to the front a cobblelock driveway with electronically operated gates provides valuable secure off-street parking.\r\n\r\nMore about the location...\r\n\r\nThe location is exceptional. Durham Road is within easy walking distance of both Sandymount Village and Sandymount Strand, offering the best of coastal living while remaining remarkably convenient to Dublin city centre.\r\n\r\nSandymount Village provides an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and everyday amenities, while nearby recreational facilities include West Wood Club, Railway Union Sports Club, the RDS and Aviva Stadium. Sydney Parade DART station and numerous bus services provide excellent transport connections, with Ballsbridge, Grand Canal Dock and the city centre all within easy reach. The area is also exceptionally well served by many of Dublin's leading schools.\r\n\r\nA superb modern Dublin 4 home combining approximately 1,905 sq. ft. of bright, beautifully proportioned accommodation, secure parking and a fantastic location close to Sandymount Village and the sea."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway (4.79m x 1.93m)\r\nWelcoming entrance hall with timber flooring, under-stair storage, alarm panel and intercom, with access to the guest WC and open-plan living/kitchen/dining accommodation.\r\n\r\nGuest WC (1.90m x 1.61m)\r\nWith tiled flooring, WC, wash hand basin, illuminated mirror and heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nLiving/Kitchen/Dining Room (6.83m x 6.63m)\r\nSuperb open-plan living/kitchen/dining space with timber flooring throughout, access to the rear garden and utility room. The kitchen with an island is fully fitted with a comprehensive range of high-end appliances including Neff induction hob, Neff dishwasher, Falmec extractor fan, Neff oven and integrated microwave, full-height Electrolux fridge and freezer and Quooker tap. There is ample pull-out storage and a feature fireplace shown in the living area.\r\n\r\nUtility Room (1.94m x 1.91m)\r\nFitted with Miele washing machine and separate dryer, Logic boiler and Joule 500L hot water cylinder.\r\n\r\nRear Garden (10.03m x 7.71m)\r\nLow-maintenance east facing rear garden with timber-effect tiling and access to the rear garden room.\r\n\r\nStorage Room (2.46m x 1.78m)\r\nUseful rear storage room with wired for electricity.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (3.72m x 2.19m)\r\nFront-facing bedroom with timber flooring and inset lighting.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (3.40m x 2.61m)\r\nFront-facing bedroom with carpet flooring, built-in wardrobes and inset lighting.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (5.25m x 2.76m)\r\nGenerous bedroom with carpet flooring, built-in wardrobes and access to the en-suite.\r\n\r\nEn-suite (3.11m x 1.19m)\r\nFully tiled with double shower cubicle with rainfall shower, WC, wash hand basin, mirrored cabinet and heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom (3.52m x 1.68m)\r\nFully tiled with bath, separate shower enclosure with rainfall shower setting, WC, wash hand basin, illuminated mirror and heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nStorage (1.10m x 0.80m)\r\nUseful storage space with shelving.\r\n\r\nSecond Floor\r\n\r\nPrincipal Bedroom (5.68m x 3.27m)\r\nExcellent principal bedroom with carpet flooring, two Velux windows providing plenty of natural light and inset lighting.\r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe (4.28m x 1.45m)\r\nExcellent storage space with wall-to-wall wardrobes, carpet flooring and access to the en-suite.\r\n\r\nPrincipal En-suite (4.60m x 1.54m)\r\nTiled flooring and part-tiled walls with Duravit double wash hand basin, WC, heated towel rail and walk-in shower with rainfall shower."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Contemporary family home extending to approximately 177 sq. m.\r\nBuilt in 2012 and arranged over three floors.\r\nB energy rating.\r\nSuperb open-plan living, kitchen and dining accommodation.\r\nHigh-end fitted kitchen with Neff and Electrolux appliances.\r\nFour generous bedrooms.\r\nPrincipal bedroom with walk-in wardrobe and en-suite.\r\nLow-maintenance rear garden.\r\nPrivate cobble lock driveway with electronically operated gates.\r\nOff-street parking.\r\nEV charging point.\r\nGas-fired central heating.\r\nGigabit fibre broadband and Cat 6 network cabling throughout.\r\nExcellent natural light throughout."
      },
